A||||7||Jncomutt||Pulling Right,  I think I found the problem||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||11-10-2001||01:31 PM||||Well I was under my car today inspecting the brake lines (I just switched to Earls) Makin sure there were no leaks or such.  What I found was that my pass. side shock absorber was all oily?  The bottom half was covered and the part it bolts to on the bottom had like drips of this fluid.  This means its blown? and would cause the pull to the right????  This correct??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jncomutt||11-10-2001||02:14 PM||||ok, I have another question.  How do I know if a shock is bad otherwise.  I have a pair I just took off my parts car.  They're yellow monroe Gas-matics.  Thing is, I can compress them with my hands and they expand back very slowly.  These are shot too... or is this just them?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||11-10-2001||03:15 PM||||If the shock/strut is bleeding, it's SHOT. It can cause some drifting problems on rough road, but not a full-time gen-u-wine pull... ||||reg||3
Z||000003||Jncomutt||11-10-2001||04:33 PM||||Hmm... Thanks Mach.  Guess my search will go on.   ||||reg||1
Z||000004||shark93726||11-10-2001||06:12 PM||||Try grabbing the rear wheel at the front and back edge of the tire, and see if you can push or pull it very much to change toe-in.  If either side can be toed significantly different this way, you have worn rubber bushings in that A-arm.<P>Also, site from the back of the car past the outside edge of the rear tire sidewalls, and see where that sight-line hits on the front tires.  It should line up with the edge of the front tire sidewalls equally on both sides of the car.  (The sight-line may point at a spot from 1/2 to 1 inch inward on the front tires, that would indicate 1/16" to 1/8" toe-in, which is ok, the main thing is that both sides of the car are equal.  If not, the car WILL pull one direction under throttle, and the other way off-throttle.) <P>Hope this helps ya.  It is what was wrong with mine, exasct same symptoms.<P>Gerald Storvik<P>------------------<BR>Gerald Storvik||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jncomutt||11-11-2001||12:10 AM||||I'll be sure to check that in the morning.  You see the weird thing is, when I go forward, the steering wheel like turns right as the car pulls.  But when i'm reverse, say backing out of a long driveway, The steering turns left, as the car pulls.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||11-11-2001||06:41 AM||||that for sure sounds like worn bushings, more so on the right side. Letting the A arm slide back n forth changing the caster.||||reg||1
Z||000007||avengador1||11-11-2001||09:29 AM||||Make sure you check your tire pressure also. If the pressure is low on one side it will tend to pull to that side (front tires).<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
